#X text 240 83 the object routes messages with a selector (any messages)
to the first outlet \, and bangs \, floats \, symbols and lists to
the second outlet;
#X text 240 138 this is useful when a patch needs to handle generic
messages separately from plain values;
#X text 240 178 the object can be used to separate control messages
from audio-rate values \, for example to route "note" messages to a
synth and plain numbers to a display;
